-16|0@Terraria^1440190152#cub3ij2:BCProgramming$:&gt; Mojang has a long history of making promises and not delivering on them. Mojang/Notch/etc have never *promised* any features. "I will eventually add X" is not a promise to add X. A promise is an additional *assurance* that something will be done, not a statement of intent. If I tell somebody, "I'll be there around 5" And don't show up, I've not broken a promise because I never made one. That is why people ask for additional assurance in some cases. Personally I'm fine with Vanilla. the main reason I prefer Vanilla is that my worlds actually remain intact. I've had to abandon a good 3 or 4 modded worlds either because of bugs or crashes or because there was no upgrade path to a more recent version.
