-1|0@Terraria^1440223645#cubkjif:longbowrocks$:Changing is different from getting more content. Pokemon gets content, but comparatively little change. In Terraria, you go fight mobs for equipment. Once your equipment is strong enough, you fight harder mobs for better equipment. Patch 1.1 was even harder mobs for even stronger equipment. Patch 1.2 was mobs even harder than *that*, and so on. The game went from fighting bosses, to fighting more bosses. Minecraft used to be about exploration and building pretty homes. Everything was static. Suddenly pistons came along and you could make secret entrances, elevators, self-assembling homes, floodgates, automatic sorting systems, etc. The world really opened up. Slime blocks upped that again by allowing structures to move themselves. This not only vastly increased the size of the contraptions you could build, but also made it possible to make custom vehicles and automatic miners. The game went from being about making something big, to making something clever.
