4|0@Terraria^1440224197#cubkpim:alanydor$:I agree with this. Each has its positives and negatives. Minecraft, for one, is much better suited to maps that resemble a cross between Ninja Warrior and Wipeout, while Terraria is mostly all about aesthetics and RPG-map building, which it does well due to its 2D side-scrolling style. Conversely, Minecraft's combat boils down to "Hit enemies with sticks. Also fuck skeletons, and have everything be diamonds all the way down," while Terraria is all about what weapons have which hitboxes, and what styles are the most effective, which delves down into, at this point, 5 different cliques of weapon damage, a TON of accessories, of which you can choose five (six in expert) to actually use, and, as I'm sure most of us know, the list goes on. Honestly though, I prefer Terraria's focus on combat to Minecraft's focus on house building and diamonds any day.
