1|0@Terraria^1440206095#cubcfkc:bubbakill7$:Honestly, the dumbest question you could ever ask. Terraria is a better game. All Minecraft does is drop you off in a world with no goals but to survive, it really isn't a game, it's just a sandbox as to which to do whatever you want. Terraria has mutliple goals and levels of progression with rising difficulty, if you were to compare Minecraft to Terraria gameplay-wise, Terraria would always win. Terraria has much more content and is much more difficult than Minecraft. I know that it sounds like I hate Minecraft, but in reality, Minecraft is great. I've spent hundreds of hours building in Minecraft but Minecraft technically isn't a game, it's more of a platform for creativity than a game. Terraria is an actual game because it has goals and challenges. In Minecraft you could go for hours before needing to ever even see a zombie and you can even disable combat.
