5|0@Terraria^1440211559#cubfbal:A_BEAUTIFUL_PONY$:The entire premise of the two games is 100% different though. Like, Minecraft is a strictly creative game. All the "goals" and opinions on what should be done are completely player imposed. You could consider yourself finished once you've built a pretty nice house. You could consider yourself finished when you have the best gear you can get. Etc. You're not directed at all and the world is simply dropped into your lap to do whatever the hell pleases you. Terraria is almost entirely different to that. I'd say the only similarities are that you mine, build and fight, and the ways each of these are done are so different that it's not a similar experience. You have some pretty definite goals (progress towards the harder fights, basically) and there's progression that's very complex and personalized. Basically it's a stupid comparison to make. Like, which is better, Ratchet &amp; Clank or Splatoon? 
